    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3322" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ărăchōsĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀραχωσία</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A province of the Persian kingdom</i>, <i>separated from India by the Indus</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6,
				23, 25</span></i>,  § 82.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ără-chōsĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Arachosia</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 13,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ărăchōtae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., the same,
					<i><span class="en">Prisc. Perieg. 1003</span></i>.</div>
